  "DELETE /v1/programs/{id}": {"key": "DELETE /v1/programs/{id}", "method": "DELETE", "path": "/v1/programs/{id}", "tag": "project", "summary": "Soft-delete a program, UN-ASSIGNING every project in it", "params": [{"name": "id", "in": "path", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string"}}], "description": "The iteration-delete rule, applied one level up: `programId` is nullable and \"in no program\" is an ordinary state, so removing the container has a defined outcome. Refusing instead would strand the workspace behind a program it had to empty by hand, one board at a time. The sweep is NOT reach-filtered — the authority is the workspace D verb, and half-emptying it would leave boards pointing at a container nothing can show — so the response is a COUNT, never the boards. Requires the workspace’s projects D verb.\n\nReplaces DELETE /project/programs/{id}.", "responses": [{"status": "200", "description": "Deleted", "contentType": "application/json", "schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Deleted"}}, {"status": "401", "description": "Error", "contentType": "application/json", "schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/StripeError"}}, {"status": "403", "description": "Error", "contentType": "application/json", "schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/StripeError"}}, {"status": "404", "description": "Error", "contentType": "application/json", "schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/StripeError"}}], "security": ["bearerAuth"], "family": ["DELETE /v1/programs/{id}", "GET /v1/programs", "GET /v1/programs/{id}", "POST /v1/programs", "POST /v1/programs/{id}"]},
